DaSessionOutputController: serve the push_file download URL

push_file stages a file into {workspace root}/{session segment}/output/ and
returns downloadUrl from deepanalyze.push.download-url-template, by default
/api/sessions/{sessionId}/output/{fileName}. Upstream, the TS backend serves
that route from the shared volume; a standalone engine has no such route, so
every link push_file returns is dead and a host cannot fetch the file.

GET (and HEAD) /api/sessions/{sessionId}/output/{fileName} now streams it:

1. Access as in DaCompatController. With deepanalyze.auth.enabled the
   X-Engine-Secret header is compared in constant time (401
   {"error":"unauthorized"}). X-Da-Session-Id (or ?sessionId=) must equal the
   session in the path; when missing and require-session-binding is on -> 404.
   X-Da-Tenant-Id is not checked: session workspaces are per session only.
   The secret check is in the controller because DaServiceAuthFilter is
   registered on /api/agents/* only (and was reworked on newer common);
   upstream should add /api/sessions/ to the filter instead.

2. Same directory as push_file. DaSessionWorkspace.sessionRoot applies the
   session-segment rule (safeSegment) to the session id in the URL, so the URL
   push_file returned resolves as is (e.g. session "t1:a" -> t1_a/output/).

3. Containment. The name must be one segment (no / or \, not . or .., not a
   *.staging temp of a publish in progress). After resolving links the file
   must sit directly in the real output directory, output itself must not be
   a link and the session directory must be inside the workspace root.
   Anything else -> 404 {"error":"File not found"}, without saying why.

4. Response. attachment with an ASCII filename plus an RFC 5987 filename*
   (Chinese names survive), Content-Type by extension (text types get
   charset=UTF-8), X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff and CSP sandbox so HTML or
   SVG never runs under the engine's origin. Range requests (206 / 416) are
   handled by Spring's Resource support.

Applies to solution b70a00246 (after 0001-0003), 0eed3c7e0 (after 0001 and
0002) and common as of 2026-11-16. Applied by deploy/compose/da/build.sh
until fixed upstream (agent-solution common).

